<%# locals: rating, count: nil
    Shared by markedsplass listings and takeaway restaurants.

    Kaufland.de's rating row: five 16px stars filled to the average, then the
    review count in 13px. The fill is the average as a share of five, handed to
    the stylesheet as a custom property; the label reads it as words. %>
<% share = (rating.to_f / 5 * 100).clamp(0, 100).round %>
<span class="store-stars" style="--rating: <%= share %>%">
  <span role="img" aria-label="<%= t("storefront.rating_of_five", rating: number_with_precision(rating, precision: 1)) %>"></span>
  <%= tag.small "(#{number_with_delimiter(count)})" if local_assigns[:count] %>
</span>
